    <string name="privilege_setup_title">Privilege setup</string>
    <string name="privilege_setup_intro">Privileged actions (silent install, later cache clean / debloat) need Shizuku or ShizukuPlus. Without it, Kiln stays on Tier NONE with system dialogs.</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_a">A · Not installed</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_b">B · Installed, not running</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_c">C · Running, no permission</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_d">D · Ready</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_a_body">Install Shizuku (or ShizukuPlus). Prefer the official GitHub release for sideload builds.</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_b_body">Start Shizuku via Wireless debugging (Android 11+), the manager app, or ADB from a PC. Then return here.</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_c_body">Grant Kiln access in the Shizuku permission dialog. If you chose “Never ask again”, open the manager app and allow Kiln manually.</string>
    <string name="privilege_phase_d_body">Shizuku is ready. Run the self-test to confirm shell UID and the capability matrix.</string>
    <string name="privilege_hyperos_hint">HyperOS/MIUI: enable “USB debugging (Security settings)” if wireless pairing fails; allow autostart and disable battery restrictions for Shizuku so the service survives sleep.</string>
